---
title: "tokenSupplyAndClaim (High Level Sale Customer Journey)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_results: project initiates token supply
    q_check_results --> q_calc_supply: results published = true
    q_check_results --> q_revert_no_results: results not published
    q_revert_no_results --> [*]: revert ResultsNotPublished
    q_calc_supply --> q_calc_fees: totalTokens = tokensAllocated
    q_calc_fees --> q_transfer_tokens: fees = legionFee + referrerFee
    q_transfer_tokens --> q_mark_supplied: transferFrom(project, sale, totalTokens + fees)
    q_mark_supplied --> q_tokens_available: tokensSupplied = true
    q_tokens_available --> q_investor_claim: investors can now claim
    q_investor_claim --> q_verify_merkle: claimTokenAllocation(merkleProof, allocation)
    q_verify_merkle --> q_check_vesting: Merkle proof valid
    q_verify_merkle --> q_revert_proof: invalid proof
    q_revert_proof --> [*]: revert InvalidMerkleProof
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: allocation has vesting schedule
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: no vesting, direct claim
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_to_vesting: deploy VestingContract for investor
    q_transfer_to_vesting --> q_mark_settled: transfer tokens to vesting contract
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark_settled: transfer tokens to investor
    q_mark_settled --> [*]: hasSettled[investor] = true

    note right of q_verify_merkle
        INV-001: Token supply must include correct fee amounts
        INV-002: Merkle proof must be verified before any token transfer
        INV-003: Vesting contracts deployed per-investor for time-locked allocations
        INV-004: Each investor can claim allocation exactly once (hasSettled guard)
    end note
